{
  "_note": [
    "Data, not code: every repo, filename and byte count below was read off the",
    "HuggingFace API on 2026-08-15, and every `dest` is the exact path the",
    "matching constant in server.py looks for (ANIMA_CLIP, ANIMA_VAE_CANDIDATES,",
    "ZIMAGE_CLIP, QWEN_EDIT_MODEL, ...). A model that lands one folder off is a",
    "model Pixal cannot see, so change these two together or not at all.",
    "",
    "`satisfied_by` is the other half of that: what ALREADY counts as installed.",
    "Two different rules, because server.py has two.  `paths` is for text",
    "encoders and VAEs, which _catalog_has() matches by exact relative path -",
    "the list is the constant's own candidate tuple, no more.  `any_path` is for",
    "diffusion models, which model_profile() classifies by NAME as well as",
    "folder, so any file the classifier would file under this family counts",
    "wherever it sits.  Paths are matched lowercased with forward slashes.",
    "",
    "`stray` names the file when it is on disk somewhere Pixal will not look:",
    "the tidy step moves those into `dest`, and nothing else is ever moved.",
    "",
    "`beside`: \"<sibling dest>\" pins a file to the FOLDER its sibling was",
    "found in (the sibling's own `dest` folder when the sibling is nowhere, so",
    "a fresh install changes nothing). It counts as installed only in that",
    "folder; a match anywhere else is a stray the tidy moves there. For files",
    "server.py discovers by the model's own folder, never by a fixed path -",
    "the chat brain's mmproj projector is the one case."
  ],

